Checkpoint 01: Select relevant variables

Create a df with id, meovrwrk, and sex. Then, use zap_missing(), as_factor(), and droplevels() to make them into clean factor variables.


# Categorical Variables
my_cat &lt;- gss22 |&gt;
  select(id, meovrwrk, sex, marital) |&gt;
  zap_missing() |&gt;
  as_factor() |&gt;
  droplevels()


Create a df with id, lifenow, and educ. Then, use mutate() and as.numeric() to make them numerical variables.


# Continuous Variables
my_con &lt;- gss22 |&gt;
  select(id, lifenow, educ) |&gt;
  mutate(
    lifenow = as.numeric(lifenow))


Combine the two dataframes and name it my_data.


# Combine the two dataframes
my_data &lt;- left_join(my_cat, my_con, by = "id")
